# Admin web

- Generate admin API types from `docs/api/admin.yaml` into `apps/admin_web/src/types/generated/admin-api.generated.ts`. Do not hand-edit the file. Run `npm run generate:admin-api-types` and `npm run check:admin-api-types` when the spec or client types change. [why: hand-written types drifted from the spec]
- Call admin APIs through `adminApiRequest` in `src/lib/api-admin-client.ts`. Responses have no `{ data }` envelope. [why: clients wrapped a body the backend does not send]
- Build list paths with `buildAdminListPath`. Page size is `ADMIN_LIST_PAGE_SIZE`; the cap is `ADMIN_API_MAX_LIST_LIMIT`. One `src/lib/<resource>-api.ts` module per resource. [why: each screen invented its own query string]
- Read server state with the shared TanStack Query client and `adminQueryKeys`. Do not hand-roll fetch loops. Hooks live in `src/hooks/`. [why: module caches and ad-hoc keys diverged]
- Navigation order is Dashboard, then Assets, Audit, Calendar, Contacts, Finance, Sales, Services, Tags, Website. The default landing route stays Finance. [why: agents reordered the shell and changed the landing page]
- In-area view switchers use `AdminTabStrip` as a button group, not ARIA tabs. [why: partial tab markup without panels]
- Styling lives in CSS classes. No `style`, no `CSSProperties`, and no inline `<svg>` in feature components. Icons are SVGR imports from `src/components/icons/svg/`. [why: eslint]
- Read `.cursor/skills/admin-crud-screen/SKILL.md` before adding or changing a list, filter, editor, or row action. [why: agents reintroduced modals, titled cards, and Apply buttons]
